{"text": "Halloran & Mirzaei Injury Lawyers - New Client Intake (Motor Vehicle)\n\nIntake no. HM-INT-26-0388. Completed by Keisha Bellamy, paralegal, on 06/17/2026. Conflict check cleared 6/18. Responsible attorney: Farida Mirzaei (BPR No. 031877).\n\n1. Client\n\nQuestion\tAnswer\n\nFull legal name\tDelphine Marie Ruvalcaba\n\nGoes by\tDel\n\nDate of birth\t11/02/1988\n\nSSN (last 4 only)\t5134\n\nDriver license\tTN 104772968\n\nHome address\t2906 Dodson Avenue, Apt 4, Chattanooga, TN 37406\n\nCell\t423-555-0171 (text OK)\n\nEmail\tdelruvalcaba88@inboxmail.example\n\nEmployer\tSaltgrass Linen & Uniform Co., route driver, $19.75/hr\n\n2. Crash\n\nQuestion\tAnswer\n\nDate and time\tFriday, June 5, 2026, about 3:40 pm (school pickup)\n\nLocation\tBrainerd Road at Germantown Road, Chattanooga, Hamilton County\n\nPolice\tChattanooga Police Department, report no. 26-058117, Ofc. R. Standifer, badge 1147\n\nCitation\tOther driver cited, failure to yield, Tenn. Code Ann. § 55-9-602 (citation E4471902)\n\nWeather\tDry, clear\n\nWitness\tYolanda Ruvalcaba (client's sister-in-law), following in her own car, (423) 555-0109\n\n3. Vehicles\n\nOur client\tOther driver\n\nDriver\tDelphine Ruvalcaba\tCurtis Pettigrew, DOB 3/9/71\n\nYear/make/model\t2019 Honda Odyssey\t2021 Ford F-150, lettered \"Pettigrew Fence & Deck\"\n\nPlate\tTN 7K4-2BN\tGA CTP4418\n\nVIN\t5FNRL6H78KB041937\t1FTEW1EP4MFA62285\n\nOwner\tclient; lien with her credit union\tPettigrew's business\n\nDamage\tTotal loss per carrier, $17,850 ACV offered\tfront end, drivable\n\n4. Injured Persons\n\nPerson\tAge / seat\tInjuries\tTreated at\n\nDelphine\t37, driver\tcervical strain; left wrist sprain; headaches since\tScenic City Urgent Care on 6/6/26\n\nMateo Ruvalcaba\t9, rear passenger side\tdisplaced fracture of the left clavicle; mild concussion, Glasgow Coma Scale 15 on arrival\tMarrowbone Valley Children's Hospital ER, same day\n\nMateo was born August 30, 2016 and is in the 4th grade at Tolland Street Elementary. He was belted in a booster. He has asthma and uses albuterol as needed. Orthopaedic follow-up is with Dr. Olusegun Bankole (NPI 1730482296); sling for 4 weeks, re-X-ray July 2; closed treatment billed as CPT 23500. Hospital MRN MV-00648213. Dr. Bankole says no contact sports until cleared. Mateo missed the last 3 days of school and the whole swim season.\n\n5. Insurance\n\nCarrier\tPolicy / claim\tLimits\tAdjuster\n\nClient\tWexford Mutual Auto Insurance Co.\tpol. WMA-TN-4418207-03; claim 26-TN-0077139\t25/50 liability, UM 25/50, MedPay $5,000\tnot yet assigned\n\nOther driver\tPendragon Casualty Company\tclaim PCC-9920-481553\tunknown; commercial policy\tLorna Tibbets, 615.555.0136, ltibbets@pendragoncasualty.example\n\nMedical\tTennCare (both)\tmember ID ZEC774190233 (Delphine); ZEC774190241 (Mateo)\n\nMs. Tibbets called the client on June 9 asking for a recorded statement and offered $1,500 \"for the inconvenience.\" Client declined. Do NOT let Pendragon contact her again; letter of representation goes out 6/19/2026.\n\n6. Staff notes\n\n- Lost wages: off work June 8 through June 19, 2 weeks at roughly $790 gross per week. Get wage verification from Saltgrass HR.\n\n- Medical bills so far: ER $6,412.30; urgent care $385; ortho visit $298.00. Both are on TennCare, so expect a subrogation lien; send Form HS-0114 request.\n\n- Client is a single parent; Mateo's father is not involved. Minor settlement will need court approval and a guardian ad litem if over the threshold.\n\n- Statute: one year, Tenn. Code Ann. § 28-3-104, so calendar 06/05/2027 for Delphine. Calendar it for Mateo too even though his claim is tolled.\n\n- Fee: 33 1/3% explained and signed (Rule 1.8). Photos uploaded to https://files.halloranmirzaei.example/intake/HM-INT-26-0388.\n\n- KB to order the crash report and the body-cam footage.", "kind": "Web page", "detail": "543 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Delphine Marie Ruvalcaba", "Delphine Ruvalcaba", "Curtis Pettigrew", "Yolanda Ruvalc